+/// argument, no cutoff, no tier and no exception: `REPORT-3a8c05.md` §2
+/// derived it as a function of per-clue structure only, and §3 bounded
+/// the whole family of monotone objectives at rank 1,127 for the
+/// canonical case-2 tuple *with* this axis in it, so nothing is gained by
+/// embellishing it.
+fn word_count_parsimony(clue_words: usize, target_words: usize) -> f64 {
+    let target = target_words.max(1);
+    1.0 - clue_words.abs_diff(target) as f64 / clue_words.max(target) as f64
